.\" Generated from cmd/vif/usage.go by TestGeneratedFilesAreTheHelpTable; do not edit.
.TH VIF 6 "" vif
.SH NAME
vif \- a modal\-motion arcade game
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B vif
.RI [ flags ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Without flags,
.B vif
starts a solo game in the terminal.
The flags below also host, join or serve a networked session,
replay or script a run, play a bot, and validate the installed configuration.
.PP
Each resource resolves from its own flag, then
.BR \-config\-dir ,
then the user configuration root, then each system root,
and finally the copy compiled into the binary.
The first root holding a
.I vif.toml
supplies the defaults of the path flags and the audio buffer;
a flag given on the command line wins.
.SH OPTIONS
.SS Session
.TP
.B \-host <addr>
Play at once and open the game to participants, e.g. :7777 or ws://:7777
.TP
.B \-serve <addr>
Bind a headless session with no local cursor, e.g. :7777 or ws://:7777
.TP
.B \-join <addr>
Join a session at [tcp://|vif://]host:port[/name] or a ws(s):// URL, or a new one an http(s):// site creates; tcp when no scheme is given
.TP
.B \-name <name>
Name this host answers to, so one address can serve several sessions
.TP
.B \-players <n>
Roster ceiling including self, 2..16; unset holds the whole roster; with a \-join site, the one requested
.TP
.B \-authority host|migrate
Where authorship goes when the authoring participant leaves; default host with \-serve, migrate otherwise
.TP
.B \-slow\-window <dur>
Window a participant's lateness is judged over; host only, 0 never evicts (default 20s)
.TP
.B \-slow\-late <n>
Evict at this many late epochs per second over the window; 0 ignores lateness (default 5)
.TP
.B \-slow\-bytes <n>
\&...and at least this many bytes per second on its link; 0 ignores throughput (default 8192)
.TP
.B \-listen <addr>
Address this participant is dialled back on; \-join only, default the host's port then an ephemeral one
.TP
.B \-no\-advertise
Keep this participant's address out of the session; \-join only, and it is never elected
.TP
.B \-size <WxH>
Terminal\-equivalent size for a run that has no terminal
.TP
.B \-probe <addr>
Health and metrics endpoint; \-serve only
.TP
.B \-first\-join <dur>
Exit if no guest connects within this; \-serve only, 0 waits forever
.TP
.B \-empty <dur>
Exit this long after the last guest leaves; \-serve only, 0 keeps the session
.TP
.B \-drain <dur>
How long a termination signal waits for an empty roster; \-serve only, 0 exits at once
.SS Configuration
.TP
.B \-d, \-config\-embedded
Use the embedded scenario and content, ignoring \-s and \-f
.TP
.B \-config\-dir <dir>
Configuration root holding scenario/ input/ audio/ content/ image/ bot/
.TP
.B \-s, \-config\-scenario <name|path>
Installed scenario name, scenario.toml, or a scenario directory
.TP
.B \-f, \-config\-content <path>
Content directory, or a single content file
.TP
.B \-k, \-config\-keymap <path>
Keymap TOML
.TP
.B \-config\-music <path>
Music pattern override TOML
.TP
.B \-config\-sounds <path>
Sound definition override TOML
.SS Presentation and audio
.TP
.B \-color auto|256|true
Colour depth; auto detects the terminal
.TP
.B \-mute[=false]
Start muted, which is the default; \-mute=false starts with sound
.TP
.B \-ab, \-audio\-backend <name>
Force an audio backend instead of detecting one
.SS Run
.TP
.B \-seed <n>
Root RNG seed; 0 draws one and logs it
.TP
.B \-speed <rate>
Simulation rate 1/8 1/4 1/2 1 2 4 8; with \-script or \-bot also "max" for no wall pacing
.TP
.B \-script <path>
Run an authored deterministic TOML tick script
.TP
.B \-bot <name|path>
Play this instance's own seat with a bot graph instead of the terminal
.TP
.B \-watch
Present a \-script or \-bot run on this terminal instead of running it headlessly
.TP
.B \-replay <path>
Replay a recorded journal instead of playing
.TP
.B \-check
Validate the resolved scenario, keymap, audio and content, then exit
.TP
.B \-schema
Print the FSM schema as JSON, then exit
.SS Diagnostics
.TP
.B \-l, \-log[=DIR]
Enable logging; DIR overrides $XDG_STATE_HOME/vif/log
.TP
.B \-lv, \-log\-level <level>
trace, debug, info, warn or error; implies \-l
.TP
.B \-ls, \-log\-scope <spec>
Which subsystems log; see Scopes below; implies \-l
.TP
.B \-lt, \-log\-stat <ticks>
Status snapshot period in game ticks, 0 disables; implies \-l
.TP
.B \-lr, \-log\-recorder <ticks>
Flight recorder depth in game ticks, 0 disables; implies \-l
.TP
.B \-log\-session\-id <id>
Attach a session ID to every application log record; implies \-l
.TP
.B \-log\-stdout
Write the log to stdout as JSON instead of to a file; implies \-l
.TP
.B \-j, \-journal[=DIR]
Record a replay journal; DIR overrides $XDG_STATE_HOME/vif/journal
.TP
.B \-mw, \-music\-wav[=DIR]
Record the music alone, as it plays, to a WAV file; DIR overrides $XDG_STATE_HOME/vif/music
.TP
.B \-dev[=false]
Capture runtime stderr to a file; on by default for \-race builds
.SS Help
.TP
.B \-h, \-help
Print this and exit
.TP
.B \-version
Print the module version and commit a package should report
.SS Scopes (\-ls)
.nf
  Names     app  fsm  event  dispatch  push  input  stat  rec  lock  tap
  Letters   a    f    e      d         p     i      s     r    l     t
  Sets      all is every scope, none is nothing
  Combine   join names or letters with + or , \[u2014] "app+fsm+stat" and "afs" are one set
  Adjust    lead with + or \- to add to or remove from the set already selected
.fi
.SH FILES
.TP
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/vif
User configuration root, normally
.IR ~/.config/vif .
.TP
.I vif.toml
Settings at the top of a configuration root: another root, the log, journal,
music, scenario, content and keymap paths, and the audio mixer buffer.
.TP
.I $XDG_CONFIG_DIRS/vif
System configuration roots, normally
.IR /etc/xdg/vif ,
and on FreeBSD
.I /usr/local/etc/xdg/vif
before it.
.TP
.I $XDG_STATE_HOME/vif
Logs and journals, normally
.IR ~/.local/state/vif .
.SH SEE ALSO
https://github.com/lixenwraith/vif
